& [ConceptualModel] distinguishes label, support, form, and proof
  + InventoryConsistencyEvidence is a closed semantic label for the kind of support a future issuer claims to possess
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual is the weakest selected label for two actual complete ordered acquisitions whose comparable canonical commitments are equal
  + OsSnapshotProven is a reserved stronger label whose provenance representation is not yet defined
  + TopologyReceipt is a pure caller-constructible form containing exactly one evidence label among its existing bounded claims
  + receipt validation proves syntax and internal relations only
  + a future acquisition envelope must own the two actual acquisition lineages
  + a future issuer proof must bind the acquisition envelope, equality evidence, receipt content, and issuer authority
  + a future consumer decision must independently check issuer, freshness, single-use, policy, and current operational preconditions

& [DataIdentities] remain role separated
  + [machine_forms_schema_identity] is cantor-phase3-machine-forms/0.2
  + [topology_forms_schema_identity] is cantor-phase3-topology-forms/0.3
  + [topology_receipt_schema_identity] is cantor-phase3-topology-receipt/0.3
  + [scanner_contract_identity] remains cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + [evidence_type_identity] is the Rust and schema name InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + [weak_evidence_value_identity] is NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual plus non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal
  + [reserved_snapshot_value_identity] is OsSnapshotProven plus os_snapshot_proven
  + [receipt_field_identity] is consistency_evidence
  + [physical_acquisition_identity] is absent from current data and cannot equal a digest, nonce, tick, or enum value
  + [issuer_identity] is absent from current data and cannot equal public form construction
  + [world_state_identity] is never represented by either current enum variant

& [LogicalSchemaDelta] is closed
  + remove ConsistencyClass with variants QuiescentDoubleInventory and OsSnapshotProven
  + add InventoryConsistencyEvidence with variants NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual and OsSnapshotProven
  + replace TopologyReceipt.consistency of ConsistencyClass with consistency_evidence of InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + change exactly three schema profile constants to their selected revisions
  + preserve WINDOWS_TOPOLOGY_PROFILE and every other type, field, order, relation, constant, and visibility
  + add no acquisition, snapshot, issuer, consumer, migration, or effect record

& [InventoryConsistencyEvidenceRepresentation] is exact
  + Rust derives Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, and Deserialize
  + serde rename_all is snake_case
  + serialized NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual is exactly non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal
  + serialized OsSnapshotProven is exactly os_snapshot_proven
  + deserialization accepts exactly those two strings
  + ValidatePhase3 is a pure total function over the closed enum and returns Ok for either structural value
  + no Default, Unknown, Other, alias, type synonym, string parser, From, Into, or fallback exists
  + the value has fixed enum cardinality and owns no variable-sized payload

& [TopologyReceiptRepresentation] remains bounded
  + receipt_profile is one bounded exact schema string
  + scanner_profile is one bounded exact scanner-contract string
  + candidate_root is bounded nonempty NUL-free caller text without a physical-canonicality claim
  + root_identity is one StrongFileIdentity
  + root_volume_guid_path is one syntactically canonical volume GUID path
  + admission_profile, admission_receipt_sha256, policy_sha256, scan_nonce, and ordered_inventory_sha256 remain required
  + limits is one complete TopologyScanLimits value
  + entry_count and total_file_bytes remain bounded u64 summaries
  + consistency_evidence is one required InventoryConsistencyEvidence value
  + issued_tick and expires_tick remain supplied u64 relation values without a clock observation in validation
  + field ordering changes only by replacing the evidence field in its existing semantic position

& [OwnershipModel] is pure and caller controlled
  + a caller constructs or deserializes InventoryConsistencyEvidence and TopologyReceipt values
  + strict serde owns decoded strings and nested values exactly as before
  + ValidatePhase3 borrows an evidence value immutably
  + ValidateTopologyForm borrows a receipt immutably
  + successful validation returns unit and does not wrap, stamp, sign, or consume the receipt
  + failed validation returns one owned bounded fault and leaves the borrowed value unchanged
  + no global, persistent, thread-local, platform, or external owner is introduced

& [Cardinality] is exact
  + InventoryConsistencyEvidence has exactly two representable variants
  + a TopologyReceipt has exactly one required consistency_evidence field
  + a valid TopologyReceipt 0.3 admits exactly one of the two representable variants
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual is the one admitted current receipt grade
  + OsSnapshotProven is representable but contributes zero valid current receipt instances
  + a receipt has zero embedded acquisition lineages, snapshot proofs, issuer proofs, or consumption decisions
  + a validation result has either unit success or exactly one atomic fault

& [EvidenceRelationModel] is explicit
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual semantically depends on two distinct actual complete acquisitions
  + the first acquisition completes before the second begins or another separately specified precise acquisition order is proven
  + both acquisitions share exact scanner, encoding, limits, root, policy, and comparison scope
  + each acquisition retains independent lineage and passes its own current rederivation
  + exact pure reconciliation disposition is Equal
  + none of those support edges is stored in this revision's enum or receipt
  + therefore enum selection and receipt validation never derive the evidence relation
  + a future issuer must introduce explicit data edges rather than treat the label as self-authentication

& [SnapshotRelationModel] is fail closed
  + OsSnapshotProven semantically depends on an identified platform snapshot primitive and exact provenance
  + no current field identifies the primitive, snapshot, creation event, mounted view, producer, lifetime, or acquisition relation
  + current receipt validation therefore rejects the value regardless of all other fields
  + no implicit downgrade converts OsSnapshotProven to NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + no future consumer may infer snapshot proof from enum structural validity

& [ValidationPipeline] preserves deterministic order
  + strictly deserialize a current-shaped receipt or release Json
  + require exact receipt_profile 0.3
  + require unchanged exact scanner_profile 0.1
  + validate candidate_root, root identity, and volume GUID path
  + validate admission profile, digests, nonce, and scan limits
  + require entry_count nonzero and at most maximum_entries
  + require total_file_bytes at most maximum_total_bytes
  + require consistency_evidence equal NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + require issued_tick less than expires_tick
  + require expires_tick at or before limits.deadline_tick
  + release unit success only after every predicate passes

& [StateMachine] is finite
  + [Encoded] transitions to Decoded or JsonFault
  + [Decoded] transitions to ProfileValid or ReceiptFault
  + [ProfileValid] transitions through unchanged bounded field-validation states or their established faults
  + [CountsValid] transitions to EvidenceAdmissible or ReceiptFault at consistency_evidence
  + [EvidenceAdmissible] transitions through unchanged tick relations or ReceiptFault
  + [RelationsValid] transitions to StructurallyValid exactly once
  + JsonFault, ReceiptFault, and StructurallyValid are terminal for one invocation
  + no migration, retry, fallback, repair, issuance, persistence, or consumption transition exists

& [LegacyRejectionMatrix] is data complete
  + receipt profile 0.2 in otherwise current-shaped data decodes and fails Receipt at receipt_profile
  + field consistency is unknown and fails strict JSON decoding
  + absent consistency_evidence fails strict JSON decoding
  + value quiescent_double_inventory fails closed-enum JSON decoding
  + simultaneous consistency and consistency_evidence fails unknown-field JSON decoding
  + old Rust type and variant names fail compilation rather than produce runtime data
  + historical artifacts are not current decoder inputs and retain their original byte identity

& [FaultRelations] preserve atomicity
  + malformed schema shapes and legacy field or token failures map to Json
  + wrong current-shaped receipt profile maps to Receipt with field receipt_profile
  + reserved snapshot value maps to Receipt with field consistency_evidence
  + unchanged nested validations preserve their existing fault codes and fields
  + exactly one earliest fault is released for one validation call
  + no fault embeds a partial receipt, evidence support, acquisition, reconciliation, or physical observation
  + diagnostic field and message remain within existing bounded construction rules

& [SerializationAndRoundTripModel] is strict
  + new valid receipt JSON contains consistency_evidence and never consistency
  + new valid receipt JSON contains non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal and never quiescent_double_inventory
  + current receipt serialization followed by strict deserialization preserves complete structural equality
  + enum serialization followed by deserialization preserves either exact variant
  + round-trip equality proves representation stability only and never acquisition or issuer provenance

& [VersionAndCompatibilityModel] is fail closed
  + each changed machine representation receives an exact new profile
  + unchanged scanner behavior retains its exact existing profile
  + no prefix matching, range matching, aliases, defaults, migrations, or compatibility shims exist
  + source callers must revise old Rust names explicitly
  + data callers must revise old profile, field, and token explicitly
  + predecessor proofs remain immutable historical authorities and are superseded only for current implementation meaning by replacement signatures

& [ResourceModel] has zero material growth
  + enum payload size remains fixed and contains no heap allocation
  + receipt field count and variable-sized payload count remain unchanged
  + validation performs constant additional comparison work only
  + no new collection, recursion, canonical buffer, digest computation, clone, database row, or persistent object exists
  + existing field and diagnostic bounds remain authoritative

& [EffectModel] is empty
  + all transforms are supplied-value serde, comparison, and pure validation
  + no unsafe, platform call, filesystem, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, Git runtime, model, tool, physical fixture, mutation, seal, cleanup, or promotion effect exists
  + Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock remain byte identical
  + no public effect-bearing entry point is created

& [ProvenanceModel] is layered
  + enum structural validity proves membership in a vocabulary only
  + receipt structural validity proves current syntax and internal relations only
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual meaning requires later explicit acquisition and equality support
  + OsSnapshotProven meaning requires later explicit platform snapshot support
  + issuer authority requires later explicit construction and proof
  + consumption and admission require later explicit policy, freshness, and single-use checks
  + no higher layer can be inferred from a lower layer without a separately authorized edge

& [DataQualityRules] are testable
  + exact profile constants match the three selected revisions and one unchanged scanner profile
  + enum cardinality and serialization tokens are exact
  + old public vocabulary is absent from production Rust
  + current valid receipt round-trips exactly
  + all five legacy JSON shapes fail at their specified boundary
  + OsSnapshotProven fails receipt validation at the exact field and code
  + every unrelated receipt positive and negative invariant remains unchanged
  + production diff touches exactly two modules and no dependency manifests

& [DataRisks] are controlled
  + state-claim inflation is controlled by evidence type and field names
  + atomicity inflation is controlled by the NonAtomic token
  + provenance laundering is controlled by absent conversions and explicit layer boundaries
  + snapshot inflation is controlled by current receipt rejection
  + legacy reinterpretation is controlled by strict decode and exact profiles
  + schema drift is controlled by replacement signatures and static fixtures
  + operational expansion is controlled by the zero-effect and two-module limits

& [DataDesignGate] passes
  + identity, ownership, cardinality, ordering, representation, and relations are explicit
  + validation and fault state transitions are finite and deterministic
  + legacy schema and current schema cannot be confused
  + evidence, form, producer, issuer, and consumer provenance remain separate
  + resource and effect growth are exactly bounded
  + all C01 through C24 constraints reapply without collision
  + [unresolved_data_question] is none inside the selected slice
  + [implementation_authority] is absent pending canonical authority and replacement signatures
  + [physical_authority] is absent
